-- Refinement types (widening slice 12, §2.14). `{T | pred}` on a parameter
-- is TRANSPARENT to typecheck.ml's own unification -- `TRefine`'s `repr`
-- strips straight to the base type (typecheck.ml:168), so the annotation
-- adds NO typing rule of its own; it is a proof obligation layered on top,
-- discharged by a separate post-typecheck AST walk (lib/refinecheck). For a
-- DIRECT call, that walk symbolically evaluates the argument against `pred`
-- (Z3, Int/Bool linear arithmetic + EUF, BLAKE3-cached) and only proceeds
-- past --check when the predicate is PROVABLY satisfied. `take_n(5)`
-- satisfies `_ >= 0` trivially. Reject companion: reject/t71 (`take_n(-3)`).
mod M do
  needs IO.Console
  fn take_n(n : {Int | _ >= 0}) : Int do n end
  fn main(_cap_console : Cap(IO.Console)) do
    println(int_to_string(take_n(5)))
  end
end
